                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Obstetrics and gynecology is the study of the physiological and pathological characteristics of the female reproductive system throughout a woman's life, as well as those related to pregnancy and the fetus,<br>A clinical medical discipline focused on women's health and disease prevention, encompassing obstetrics, perinatal medicine, general gynecology, and gynecological oncology<br>Women's health care, family planning, and eugenics. During the teaching process, emphasize the principle of "less but better," focusing on common gynecological and obstetric diseases<br>The disease is explained in a straightforward and concise manner, closely integrating clinical practice with ideological and political education, promoting the values of "rigor," "truth-seeking," and "dedication."<br>The medical ethics of "serving the people" convey positive and uplifting humanistic values in medicine to students, while appropriately introducing domestic and international<br>Professional Progress (January 13, 2023). Download Link: E-Learning Platform Syllabus Interface (https://elearning.fudan.edu.cn/courses/70878/assignments/syllabus)</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
